T* (That forest, how robust and rough its growth,) Tj
T* (Which to remember only, my dismay) Tj
T* (Renews, in bitterness not far from death.) Tj
T* (Yet to discourse of what there good befell,) Tj
T* (All else will I relate discover?d there.) Tj
T* (How first I enter?d it I scarce can say,) Tj
T* (Such sleepy dullness in that instant weigh?d) Tj
T* (My senses down, when the true path I left,) Tj
T* (But when a mountain?s foot I reach?d, where clos?d) Tj
T* (The valley, that had pierc?d my heart with dread,) Tj
T* (I look?d aloft, and saw his shoulders broad) Tj
T* (Already vested with that planet?s beam,) Tj
T* (Who leads all wanderers safe through every way.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Then was a little respite to the fear,) Tj
T* (That in my heart?s recesses deep had lain,) Tj
T* (All of that night, so pitifully pass?d:) Tj
