T* (Struggling with terror, turn?d to view the straits,) Tj
T* (That none hath pass?d and liv?d. My weary frame) Tj
T* (After short pause recomforted, again) Tj
T* (I journey?d on over that lonely steep,) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The hinder foot still firmer. Scarce the ascent) Tj
T* (Began, when, lo! a panther, nimble, light,) Tj
T* (And cover?d with a speckled skin, appear?d,) Tj
T* (Nor, when it saw me, vanish?d, rather strove) Tj
T* (To check my onward going; that ofttimes) Tj
